.TH HTTP_SKIP_HEADER 3
.SH NAME
http_skip_header \- find the end of the head of a response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "size_t http_skip_header(const char* " x ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_skip_header ()
returns the number of bytes at the start of the
.I len
bytes at
.I x
that make the head of a message: everything up to and including the empty line that ends the headers.
If there is no empty line the result is
.IR len .
.SH SEE ALSO
http_get_header(3)
